{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfi7igDYfZHNN8Fd8Q57L","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The notice route now runs on state: a conditional region driven by `noticeOpen` shows the notice. `npm test` (286 passing), `npm run test:hydration`, `npm run test:e2e` (11 passing), `test:ssr` and `test:hydration-dev` all pass.\n\n[x] The notice route's server response contains no notice host when `noticeOpen` is false, and its state script says so\n[x] Clicking the show button adds one notice host to the page\n[x] Clicking dismiss removes the notice host\n[x] The notice can be opened again after being dismissed\n[x] The notice component dispatches a dismiss event and does not remove its own host (browser suite: the host is still connected after the button click when no handler acts)\n[x] The client entry contains no `addEventListener` or `innerHTML` use outside the assertions harness and reveal helper\n[x] The runtime assertions contain no FAIL\n[x] `npm test`, `npm run test:hydration`, and `npm run test:e2e` pass\n\nWhat changed:\n\n1. **Notice component** (`example-hydration/components/notice.ts`): the dismiss button now emits a `dismiss` event instead of removing its own host. It keeps `client: true` because the browser creates it.\n2. **Notice page** (`example-hydration/pages/notice.ts`): the show button's `onclick` calls `State.openNotice`. A `${() => state.noticeOpen() ? ... : ''}` region renders the notice, and its `ondismiss` calls `State.dismissNotice`. The `#notice-target` div is gone.\n3. **Client entry** (`example-hydration/client/index.ts`): the old button listener and `innerHTML` code are removed. It now has no `addEventListener` or `innerHTML` at all.\n4. **Tests:**\n   - The browser suite has a test that the notice emits without removing itself, and one that mounts the page and goes through open, dismiss, open again.\n   - The hydration suite checks there is no notice host and that `noticeOpen` is false in the state script.\n   - The e2e spec now covers reopening after dismiss, and the no-FAIL assertions check also runs on `/notice`.\n\n**Gotcha I hit:** in `test/index.ts`, pages import `microtags/htm`, which resolves to `dist/htm.browser.js`. That is a separate copy from `src/htm.browser.js`, so the src `mount` rendered the page's markup as escaped text. The page test therefore uses the `mount` from `'microtags/htm'`. I added a note about this to `AGENTS.md`.\n\n**Other notes:**\n- This worktree had no `node_modules`. I ran `npm install` and `npm run build` first; the lockfile did not change.\n- `npm run lint` reports two unused-variable errors in `test/plugins.ts`. I didn't touch that file, so I left them alone.\n- Everything went into one commit (`85d2f20`), not one per checklist item, because the items share the same few files.\n\n**Connectors:** Gmail, Google Calendar, Google Drive and Netlify need authorizing in your claude.ai connector settings before they can be used. The aws-mcp server failed to connect."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":625,"cache_read_input_tokens":66412,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":625},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"08aa63c3-315f-4fdb-885f-6929dbed4e0c","uuid":"8dca8083-9e09-4a1c-abaa-fb2bc55bccc3","timestamp":"2026-10-05T00:08:02.911Z","request_id":"req_011Cfi7ifRfrSiYEw84gTMRX"}
